BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//icalendar//mxm.dk//
NAME:🎬 SIFF (Uptown House 2)
X-WR-CALNAME:🎬 SIFF (Uptown House 2)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260515T151446Z
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Red Hangar
DTSTART:20260515T203000Z
DTEND:20260515T220500Z
DTSTAMP:20260515T203000Z
UID:6pZfmcoUrr
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 81 mins (1h21m)\n\nIn the aftermath of the 1973 Chil
 ean coup d'état\, an Air Force logistics officer is ordered to convert a 
 hangar into a detention and torture center. As repression tightens\, he is
  forced to confront obedience\, loyalty\, and the moral cost of a nation d
 escending into dictatorship.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-red-hang
 ar\n\nEstimated start: 13:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kikuyu Land
DTSTART:20260515T230000Z
DTEND:20260516T004500Z
DTSTAMP:20260515T230000Z
UID:4ELuk3rMbu
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 93 mins (1h33m)\n\nWhat begins as a seemingly straig
 htforward investigation into land restitution in Kenya leads to a web of e
 xploitation\, family secrets\, and death threats in this riveting politica
 l documentary. Producers Moses Bwayo\, Mike Morrisoe\, Mia Vyzis\; Executi
 ve Producers Barbara Terzieff and Tracy Rector\; and key participant Ngang
 a Mungai scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/kikuyu-land
 \n\nEstimated start: 16:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Teachings of the Elders
DTSTART:20260516T013000Z
DTEND:20260516T025000Z
DTSTAMP:20260516T013000Z
UID:jQfL6J1IdV
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 70 mins (1h10m)\n\nIndigenous Elders share teachings
  through story\, land\, and memory\, guiding future generations with wisdo
 m rooted in perseverance\, relationships\, and enduring cultural knowledge
  across communities. Filmmakers scheduled to attend. This shorts program 
 is generously sponsored by Crystal Wilson.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festiva
 l/teachings-of-the-elders\n\nEstimated start: 18:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Animation4Adults
DTSTART:20260516T040000Z
DTEND:20260516T054500Z
DTSTAMP:20260516T040000Z
UID:aKTftDYG8s
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 92 mins (1h32m)\n\nSome films deserve to be animated
 . These ten short films will open your visual cortex to all of the gloriou
 s possibilities in store when we tell stories through animation.\n\nhttps:
 //www.siff.net/festival/animation4adults-x41547\n\nEstimated start: 21:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Life We Leave
DTSTART:20260516T200000Z
DTEND:20260516T214000Z
DTSTAMP:20260516T200000Z
UID:Yoa2nmwvPJ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 87 mins (1h27m)\n\nAn ambitious entrepreneur and two
  funeral directors pioneer a groundbreaking eco-friendly deathcare facilit
 y in Washington state\, challenging traditional burial practices and trans
 forming end-of-life rituals.Recipient of a 2024 SIFF Grant for Courageous 
 Documentary Filmmaking. The 2026 Grant Cycle opens May 15 on the SIFF webs
 ite. Director JJ Gerber and subjects Micah Truman\, Brie Smith\, and Katey
  Houston scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-life-we
 -leave\n\nEstimated start: 13:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lady
DTSTART:20260516T223000Z
DTEND:20260517T001500Z
DTSTAMP:20260516T223000Z
UID:YX3iYelROo
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nIn this absurdly hilarious mockum
 entary\, a young filmmaker agrees to film the behind-the-scenes vanity pro
 ject of the obnoxiously entitled Lady Isabella\, only for something unseen
  and quite strange to happen.Director Samuel Abrahams scheduled to attend 
 the May 16 screening.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/lady\n\nAlso playin
 g at:\n  • Uptown House 1 (Sun 17 May\, 11:30 AM)\n\nEstimated start: 15
 :40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Big Cheese
DTSTART:20260517T011500Z
DTEND:20260517T031000Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T011500Z
UID:FVZiknLaWm
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 101 mins (1h41m)\n\nAdam “Mr. Moo” Moskowitz is 
 on a mission to make the world take American cheesemongers seriously. For 
 over a decade\, he’s led a team of eccentric misfits to the Olympics of 
 Cheese\, where Team USA has never won. Could this be their year? Director 
 Sara Joe Wolansky and Subjects Courtney Johnson & Adam Moskowitz schedul
 ed to attend. After the film on Sat\, May 16\, pass and ticket-holders ca
 n head over to Tin Lizzie for an udderly delicious cheese tasting\, courte
 sy of Street Cheese and Peterson Cheese\, with custom wine pairings availa
 ble for purchase. It will surely stink. Wink.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/fest
 ival/the-big-cheese\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Uptown House 3 (Sun 17 May\
 , 1:30 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 18:25
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fifteen
DTSTART:20260517T040000Z
DTEND:20260517T055000Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T040000Z
UID:SG7KVHxgVl
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nGrowing up is terrifying enough\,
  but for two best friends planning the ultimate quinceañera\, the real ho
 rror is what's growing inside one of them. Director Yossy Zagha scheduled 
 to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/fifteen\n\nAlso playing at:\n 
  • Downtown (Fri 15 May\, 11:59 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 21:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Strange River
DTSTART:20260517T184500Z
DTEND:20260517T204500Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T184500Z
UID:vCKCOxUY6h
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 106 mins (1h46m)\n\nSixteen-year-old Dídac spends a
  summer cycling along the Danube with his family. When a mysterious boy ap
 pears\, new emotions stir\, subtly shifting family dynamics and guiding D
 ídac through a transformative journey of first love and self-discovery. T
 his film is generously sponsored by Jeff Stolz & Tim O'Connor.\n\nhttps://
 www.siff.net/festival/strange-river\n\nEstimated start: 11:55
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Body Blow
DTSTART:20260517T211500Z
DTEND:20260517T230500Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T211500Z
UID:1Xg0cXIrg5
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nDanger and desire go hand-in-hand
  as a musclebound young cop goes undercover in Sydney’s gay scene\, only
  to fall for an alluring twink fatale\, in Dean Francis’ explicit and ca
 mpy neo-noir that refracts the erotic thriller through an unapologetically
  queer lens.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/body-blow\n\nEstimated start
 : 14:25
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Powwow People
DTSTART:20260517T233000Z
DTEND:20260518T013000Z
DTSTAMP:20260517T233000Z
UID:tsHWChiaRM
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 106 mins (1h46m)\n\nPowwow People immerses us in a s
 ingle day at a powwow\, guided by Reuben Little Head’s humor and heart\,
  culminating in a long take honoring community as privilege. Director Sky 
 Hopinka (Ho-Chunk Nation/Pechanga Band of Luiseño Indians) and Impact Pro
 ducer Amber Morning Star Byars scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.ne
 t/festival/powwow-people\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Downtown (Sat 16 May\,
  2:30 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 16:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Furious
DTSTART:20260518T024500Z
DTEND:20260518T045500Z
DTSTAMP:20260518T024500Z
UID:lgcftBKvHW
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nAfter the daughter of Wang Wei (
 Xie Miao) is kidnapped by a criminal network and he receives no help from 
 the corrupt police\, Wei sets out on a rampage to find her himself. His on
 ly ally is Navin (Joe Taslim) – a relentless journalist whose wife has m
 ysteriously disappeared. Fueled by a furious vengeance\, the unlikely duo 
 ruthlessly fights against the kidnappers in this explosive martial arts sh
 owdown.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-furious\n\nEstimated start: 2
 0:00
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
